## Claim under audit

In the current eight-no-root `k=7` finite split, the last profile is

```text
C:(d_v,q,s)=(5,12,12),    d_6=5.
```

The exact seven-row obstruction claims that no compatible one-cycle lift reaches
singleton-functional extra rank eleven. That is the needed obstruction because:

1. the six-row replacement inequality gives `s_f >= 10` when `D_6=3`, `p=12`,
   and `d_6=5`; the six-row quotient has dimension ten, so a survivor must have
   full six-row functional rank ten;
2. canonical-complete blocks persist under a compatible six-to-seven lift, hence
   deficiency is monotone and `d_7 >= d_6 = 5`;
3. the established seven-row containment alternatives therefore reduce to
   `d_7=5` and singleton capacity at least eleven; and
4. the seven-row replacement inequality has `D_7=1`, `p_7=12`, `d_7=5`, so it
   requires extra rank at least eleven.

The verifier is conservative in the correct direction. For each qualifying lift
it inserts *every* compatible singleton state from every virtual-complete block,
not merely a jointly realizable all-singleton selection. Thus its computed rank is
an upper bound for any actual target. A zero count of rank-eleven lifts excludes
the actual profile, provided the finite cover is exhaustive.

