## Hostile scope checks

### Quantifiers

The computation is exhaustive over the committed 325,955-representative
six-row augmentation cover and all synchronized rank-one coefficient lines in
each representative. It is not an exhaustive search over arbitrary geometric
sources; the reduction from a global survivor to this cover belongs to the
earlier finite support-7 route and is not promoted here.

### Rank direction

The verifier subtracts the exact complete-block relation rank and includes all
compatible singleton rows. Any omission would weaken the obstruction; the stated
zero rank-eleven count is therefore used only in the over-approximating direction.

### Deficiency branch

The `d_7=4` alternative is not silently discarded: the separate monotonicity
lemma proves `C_6 subset C_7` and hence `d_7>=5`. The transcript's zero
`seven_d4_lifts` in the earlier full-span audit is a consistency check, not the
logical basis of the present closure.

### Arithmetic

The modulus is certified prime by the verifier's Lucas–Lehmer test. The note's
strict squared Hadamard bounds dominate every observed functional and relation
minor, so no probabilistic finite-field rank assumption enters the finite claim.

### Boundary and source scope

This finite obstruction never deletes contact-isolated source points and never
extends the core ZR/ZF kernel theorem to the full source. It proves only that the
specified support/profile lift cannot occur.

